    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate focused on maximizing efficiency against a slate of mediocre-to-favorable opposing starters. The strongest play on the board is **Seiya Suzuki** (75.03), who benefits from a prime slot in the two-hole and an advantageous matchup against Ed Rodriguez. His score is bolstered by a favorable park factor and, crucially, a slow opposing pitcher delivery that boosts his stolen base efficiency, a metric we prioritize heavily. Similarly, **Brice Turang** (71.26) and **Corbin Carroll** (70.87) represent high-floor staples today. While **Corbin Carroll** faces a slight penalty due to a lefty-lefty matchup, his elite speed remains a force-multiplier for our 5x5 Roto needs. **Mickey Moniak** (69.13) rounds out our most effective tier; his +14% boost from a dynamic platoon advantage against Matt Waldron makes him a must-start despite his lower base projection.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today centered on **Griffin Conine**, who fell just short of the starting cut with a score of 43.48. While his strong xwOBA of .380 made him an attractive candidate for the utility spot, the optimizer ultimately leaned toward the platoon-advantaged **Vinnie Pasquantino** (54.93). Though **Vinnie Pasquantino** faces a tougher SP_xERA of 3.24, his superior lineup position and platoon split against Spencer Miles narrowly edged out **Griffin Conine**. We are also keeping a close eye on the volatile matchup for **Max Muncy** (58.42); while he offers potential, his bottom-third batting order and the presence of a tough lefty in Connor Prielipp force us to temper expectations. Managers should monitor lineups for **Isaac Paredes**, **Max Muncy**, **Austin Riley**, **Jose Caballero**, and **Vinnie Pasquantino**, as their projected slots are subject to change. With **James Wood** and **Trevor Story** remaining sidelined, our bench depth\u2014including **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte**\u2014will be leaned upon heavily to maintain our categories through the end of August.",
